The HTTP 100 continue package was split into two parts, the first one included the headers and the second one was an EMPTY_LAST_CONTENT.  The LastHttpContent  will cause the NullPointException. See the code and Exception stack below: 

```
protected Object decode(ChannelHandlerContext ctx, HttpObject msg) throws Exception {
    if (msg instanceof HttpResponse && ((HttpResponse) msg).getStatus().code() == 100) {
        // 100-continue response must be passed through.
        if (msg instanceof ReferenceCounted) {
            // need to call retain to not free it
            ((ReferenceCounted) msg).retain();
        }
        return msg;
    }
    if (msg instanceof HttpMessage) {
        assert message == null;
        message = (HttpMessage) msg;
        decodeStarted = false;
        cleanup();
    }

    if (msg instanceof HttpContent) {
